{"name":"Golden Period","hex":"#fedb2d","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"golden","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Made of, or relating to, gold.","Having a color or other richness suggestive of gold."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["(Can we verify this sense?) brassy drummer, brassy chub, etc. (Kyphosus vaigiensis), a fish found in southeast Asia.","Ellipsis of golden retriever."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/golden"},{"term":"period","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A length of time. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","A length of time in history seen as a single coherent entity; an epoch, era."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Designating anything from a given historical era.","Evoking, or appropriate for, a particular historical period, especially through the use of elaborate costumes and scenery."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/period"}],"entries":[{"title":"Golden hour (medicine)","blocks":[{"text":"In emergency medicine, the golden hour is the period of time immediately after a traumatic injury during which there is the highest likelihood that prompt medical and surgical treatment will prevent death. While initially defined as an hour, the exact time period depends on the nature of the injury and can be more than or less than this duration. It is well established that the person's chances of survival are greatest if they receive care within a short period of time after a severe injury; however, there is no evidence to suggest that survival rates drop off after 60 minutes. Some have come to use the term to refer to the core principle of rapid intervention in trauma cases, rather than the narrow meaning of a critical one-hour time period."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/35/Golden_hour_graph.png/330px-Golden_hour_graph.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Golden_hour_(medicine)","wikidata":"Q2708761"},{"title":"Golden hour (photography)","blocks":[{"text":"In photography, the golden hour is the period of daytime shortly after sunrise or before sunset, during which daylight is redder and softer than when the sun is higher in the sky."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d2/Newbury_Racecourse_Road.jpg/330px-Newbury_Racecourse_Road.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Golden_hour_(photography)","wikidata":"Q3238843"},{"title":"Gold (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Gold, also called golden, is a color tone resembling the chemical element gold."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5b/GoldNuggetUSGOV.jpg/330px-GoldNuggetUSGOV.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gold_(color)","wikidata":"Q208045"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/ba/PlanckianLocus.png/500px-PlanckianLocus.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/ba/PlanckianLocus.png/1280px-PlanckianLocus.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/ba/PlanckianLocus.png/500px-PlanckianLocus.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The color temperature of daylight varies with the time of day. It tends to be around 2,000 K shortly after sunrise or before sunset, around 3,500 K during \"golden hour\", and around 5,500 K at midday. The color temperature can also change significantly with altitude, latitude, season, and weather conditions.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APlanckianLocus.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/23/20240920_53rd_Street_Hyde_Park_Chicago_near_equinox_stacked_rotated_and_recropped_4x3.jpg/500px-20240920_53rd_Street_Hyde_Park_Chicago_near_equinox_stacked_rotated_and_recropped_4x3.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/23/20240920_53rd_Street_Hyde_Park_Chicago_near_equinox_stacked_rotated_and_recropped_4x3.jpg/1280px-20240920_53rd_Street_Hyde_Park_Chicago_near_equinox_stacked_rotated_and_recropped_4x3.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/23/20240920_53rd_Street_Hyde_Park_Chicago_near_equinox_stacked_rotated_and_recropped_4x3.jpg/500px-20240920_53rd_Street_Hyde_Park_Chicago_near_equinox_stacked_rotated_and_recropped_4x3.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Near the equinoxes in Chicago the sunsets occur in the middle of east-west streets (an event known as Chicagohenge), creating intriguing golden hour photography opportunities like this diffraction spike in an urban canyon. Similar phenomena (such as Manhattanhenge) occur in other parts of the world at various times of the year.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A20240920_53rd_Street_Hyde_Park_Chicago_near_equinox_stacked_rotated_and_recropped_4x3.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f6/Bangkok_skytrain_sunset.jpg/500px-Bangkok_skytrain_sunset.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f6/Bangkok_skytrain_sunset.jpg/960px-Bangkok_skytrain_sunset.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f6/Bangkok_skytrain_sunset.jpg/500px-Bangkok_skytrain_sunset.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABangkok_skytrai